    donenessCue: 'Bark is dry and deep black-brown with the coriander seeds visibly cracked and toasted; a probe sinks between the muscle fibres as if pushing into softened butter, and the flat visibly droops off the tongs when lifted.',
    oilSprayRequired: false,
    proTip: 'A packaged corned beef brisket flat comes brine-cured at about 3% salt by weight — that is grocery-store deli territory, not pastrami. The 24-hour cold water soak with three water changes is not optional; without it the finished pastrami tastes like a salt lick. The finishing steam in foil (or better, in a Dutch oven with an inch of water on a rack) is what separates a Katz\'s-style sliceable pastrami from a chewy corned-beef roast.',
