      'If you\'re working from dried cannellini beans rather than canned, they need a genuine stovetop boil before going into the slow cooker. Dried beans in the kidney-bean family carry a natural compound that a slow cooker\'s LOW setting, which never produces a real rolling boil, won\'t reliably break down.',
