      'Apply the dry rub and let the rack sit uncovered in the fridge for a few hours if time allows, rather than rubbing it right before sealing the lid — the rest lets the rub tack into a thin paste on the surface, which holds up to the steam bath better than a fresh dusting that can simply rinse off into the liquid.',
      'Apple cider versus plain water mostly changes the flavor of whichever part of the coil sits closest to the pooled liquid at the bottom of the pot; that\'s a normal, minor difference in the finished rack, not something to fix by rearranging the coil partway through.',
