    technicalDeepDive: 'Outside skirt is diaphragm muscle: coarse fiber bundles laced with intermuscular fat rather than fine marbling. At roughly 3/4 inch, that fat sits close enough to the surface that direct 600°F heat renders and ignites some of it against the coals, and the resulting fat-vapor combustion is what gives skirt its distinct smokiness versus a pan sear. Because the cut is thin, radiant heat drives the surface through the Maillard range well before conduction carries much heat to the center, so a two-to-three-minute-per-side hit finishes the crust without pushing the core past 130°F. The structural connective tissue here does not need time to convert to gelatin, which is why no indirect phase is required.',
    keywords: ['how long to grill skirt steak', 'skirt steak grill time', 'skirt steak internal temperature', 'grilled skirt steak medium rare', 'skirt steak grain direction'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to grill skirt steak: ripping-hot direct, 4–6 min total to a 125°F pull. Why the grain runs across, not along.',
