    technicalDeepDive: 'These thighs go into the pot raw rather than seared, so the dish\'s meaty depth comes largely from what they release into the broth as proteins denature and fat renders during the poach. Held at a bare 200°F–210°F rather than a boil, the liquid stays gentle enough that the thighs cook through evenly without the exterior overcooking before the center catches up. Thigh meat carries more fat and connective tissue than breast, so the target runs to 175°F–180°F instead of 165°F: below that, collagen between fibers hasn\'t loosened, and forks would tear stringy strands instead of shredding cleanly. The uncovered simmer afterward concentrates dissolved gelatin and starch into a thicker body.',
