    technicalDeepDive: 'Breast is fast-twitch white muscle built for short bursts, with very little collagen or connective tissue, so its proteins simply coagulate and toughen once they clear the 165°F safety floor, with no structural fat or gristle to benefit from extra heat. Thigh is slow-twitch dark meat built for sustained movement, packed with connective tissue and myoglobin, and that collagen needs to climb well past 165°F to fully convert into gelatin, which is why 175°F reads as properly done rather than overcooked. The 400°F indirect stage cooks both pieces gently enough that the breast doesn\'t rocket past its ceiling while the thigh takes the extra time it needs, and the brief 500°F direct finish exists purely to blister and color skin that indirect heat alone would leave pale.',
    keywords: ['how long to grill spatchcock chicken', 'grilled whole chicken time', 'spatchcock chicken temperature', 'butterflied chicken grill', 'whole chicken internal temp grill'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to grill a spatchcocked whole chicken: two-zone indirect at 400°F, 40–55 min to 165°F breast / 175°F thigh. Why flat beats trussed.',
