    proTip: 'Pull the ham hock out at the 6-hour mark, strip the meat and skin off the bone on a cutting board, then return the shredded meat to the pot for the last hour — leaving the whole hock in for the entire cook makes it a nightmare to break down once the peas have thickened around it.',
