    technicalDeepDive: 'Cutting the chuck into three chunks instead of leaving it whole exposes far more of its collagen-webbed interior directly to the simmering chipotle liquid, so heat and moisture reach into the connective tissue from several faces at once rather than creeping in from one exterior surface. Chuck is a heavily worked shoulder muscle, dense with the kind of collagen that needs sustained time near a simmer to hydrolyze into gelatin, and it\'s that gelatin, not the muscle fibers themselves, that ends up carrying the richness once the meat is pulled. Lime and adobo mostly season the surface early, since acid penetrates cooked meat slowly.',
    keywords: ['how long to slow cook beef barbacoa', 'beef barbacoa slow cooker time', 'crockpot barbacoa chuck roast', 'slow cooker barbacoa tacos', 'chipotle barbacoa internal temp'],
