    verificationBasis: 'USDA FSIS 165°F poultry safe minimum; Crock-Pot 6-Qt Set & Forget manufacturer chart (boneless skinless chicken breast: LOW 3–4 hrs); the "165°F ceiling on breast, do not overshoot" guidance is documented in Cook\'s Illustrated "Slow Cooker Revolution" and in Hamilton Beach\'s own boneless-breast slow-cooker recipe cards.',
    technicalDeepDive: 'Boneless breast is nearly all fast-twitch fiber with almost no fat or collagen, so it has no reserve to fall back on once its proteins tighten and begin squeezing out moisture; a fattier, more connective cut can keep cooking past that point because rendering fat and dissolving collagen replace what\'s lost, but breast has neither to spare. Laying the four pieces flat in a single layer, fully submerged in broth, keeps every part of the meat in equally efficient conductive contact with the heat, so the thickest breast reaches the same internal temperature as the thinnest one at roughly the same moment.',
