    technicalDeepDive: 'A whole turkey breast is far more mass than a chicken breast, so heat must conduct inward through several more inches of tissue before the deepest point near the bone ever registers a rise, which is the whole reason this cook runs five to seven hours instead of three or four. Lifting the breast off the floor on foil balls lets simmering broth\'s steam circulate underneath as well as around it, so the bottom cooks by the same gentle convection reaching the top rather than sitting flush against the insert. Bone-in construction also means meat nearest the bone trails the rest, since bone conducts heat differently than muscle.',
