    flipAtMinutes: 0,
    restMinutes: 5,
    donenessCue: 'A cake tester or thin paring knife slides into the thickest potato with the same feel as pushing through soft butter — no resistance, no snap in the centre; the skins have gone leathery and matte with visible salt crust, and the potato yields like a bean bag when squeezed with tongs.',
    oilSprayRequired: false,
    proTip: 'Skip the foil wrap and skip adding water — both are holdovers from oven baked-potato recipes that do the exact wrong thing here. Foil traps steam against the skin and gives you soggy, wet potato instead of the dry-fluffy interior a russet is capable of, and any added liquid in the pot pools at the bottom and boils the underside instead of steaming the whole potato evenly in its own moisture.',
    verificationBasis: 'Idaho Potato Commission "Slow Cooker Baked Potatoes" published method (LOW 7–8 hrs / HIGH 4–5 hrs for medium russets, no foil, no water); Crock-Pot 6-Qt Set & Forget recipe archive "Baked Potatoes" (LOW 7–8 hrs); no probe target — doneness is a cake-tester slide-in test typical for whole starchy vegetables, so internalTempTargetF is intentionally omitted per HR-2.',
    technicalDeepDive: 'A whole russet is essentially a sealed package of starch granules and water, and the slow cooker\'s trapped, humid convective air heats that package gently enough for gelatinization to proceed from the outside in without the exterior ever nearing a hard boil. Because there\'s no foil and no added water, the only moisture at work is what\'s already inside each potato and what condenses on the lid, so the skin dries into a leathery casing while the starch beneath swells into a fluffy matrix. The dense flesh and intact skin slow heat penetration to the center, which is the real reason this takes seven-plus hours versus a couple hours in a hot dry oven.',
    keywords: ['how long to slow cook baked potatoes', 'crockpot baked potatoes time', 'slow cooker whole russet potatoes', 'baked potatoes low all day', 'no foil slow cooker potatoes'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to bake whole russet potatoes in the slow cooker: 7–8 hours on LOW, no foil, no water. Why the foil wrap actually ruins the interior.',
