      'There\'s a smell shift partway through: the milder, fattier smell of rendering gives way to a distinctly nuttier, sweeter aroma once the proteins and residual sugars on the lean surface actually start browning, rather than the fat just melting.',
      'Watch the very edges of each strip — the thin fat rim along the border curls and crisps into a lacy edge before the broader center of the strip catches up, since the edges have less mass and exchange heat with the surroundings faster.',
