    restMinutes: 10,
    donenessCue: 'A Thermapen driven horizontally into the widest point of the loaf reads 160°F+; the loaf holds its shape when the sling is lifted; juices at the base of the trivet run clear brown rather than pink.',
    oilSprayRequired: false,
    proTip: 'Shape the loaf into an elongated oval no more than 3 inches tall — a tall dome takes 8 extra minutes to hit 160°F in the centre while the ends overcook and go rubbery. For the finished glaze, transfer the loaf to a foil-lined sheet pan and run it under the broiler for 3 minutes; the pressure cooker crust is otherwise damp and grey.',
    verificationBasis: 'America\'s Test Kitchen "Multicooker Perfection" (2017), Meatloaf and Mashed Potatoes chapter, 25-minute HP benchmark for 1.5 lb loaf; USDA FSIS "Ground Beef and Food Safety" 160°F safe minimum internal temperature for ground beef; probe verification with ThermoWorks Thermapen One.',
    technicalDeepDive: 'Ground beef bound with a panko, egg, and milk panade behaves differently than a solid cut: the panko starch swells as it absorbs steam, trapping juices that loosely packed meat proteins would otherwise squeeze out as their fibers coagulate and tighten. Sitting above the waterline on the trivet means heat arrives by a mix of convection and conduction rather than through submerged liquid, so the loaf\'s cross-sectional thickness, not its length, is what governs how fast the center comes up to temperature. The chamber\'s elevated pressure pushes that center past the 160°F ground-beef floor while the surface stays wet from the steam, which is exactly why no crust forms without a separate dry-heat finish afterward.',
    keywords: ['how long to cook meatloaf in instant pot', 'instant pot meatloaf time', 'pressure cooker meatloaf temperature', 'instant pot meatloaf internal temp', '1.5 lb meatloaf instant pot'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to cook a 1.5 lb meatloaf in the Instant Pot: 25 mins High Pressure + 10 min NPR. Pull at 160°F internal. Broil the glaze after.',
