    proTip: 'Tri-tip has TWO grain directions in a single roast that meet at a 45° angle roughly two-thirds of the way through. Slice one section, rotate the roast, and slice the other — cutting the whole roast in one direction leaves half your slices with-the-grain and chewy. This is the "tri-tip" idiosyncrasy that most home cooks miss.',
