      'Grip the exposed end of the thigh bone with tongs and give it a gentle twist. It should rotate with very little resistance once the collagen surrounding the joint has broken down; if it still feels locked in place, that area needs more time even if the skin already looks done.',
      'Check the color of any fat pooled at the base of each thigh on the grate. It should run clear and golden rather than the cloudy, slightly pink look it has early in the cook, a sign the subcutaneous fat layer has fully rendered rather than just the surface skin coloring up.',
