      'A fully rendered pan of fat looks shallow and mostly clear, with a golden cast. Fat that\'s still cloudy or milky-white hasn\'t finished rendering yet even if the bacon on top already looks colored.',
      'The strips nearest the pan\'s raised rim firm up a minute or two ahead of the strips in the middle, since they pick up extra radiant heat reflected off the pan\'s sides.',
