      'Smell the crust before pulling it. A blackened cod crust should smell toasted and peppery; if it turns sharp or acrid, the surface spice has crossed from blackened into burnt even if the color still looks dark and even.',
      'Check the seam near where the pin bones used to run, at the thickest part of the fillet. That band is the last part of the fish to lose its gray, slightly translucent look, making it a more reliable doneness check than the edges of the fillet.',
