        q: 'Should I roast directly in the same dutch oven I seared in, or transfer to a rack?',
        a: 'Roasting directly in the same pot after searing is standard and fine. A rack keeps the underside as dry as the top since the roast won\'t sit in contact with any drippings, which matters more here than on a fattier cut since there\'s little rendered fat to begin with.',
